          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: प्रकाशः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रकाशः (prakāśaḥ) — \"light\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रकाशः (prakāśaḥ) is light: brightness itself, and the state of a thing being visible at all."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You met a piece meaning \"to shine, to be seen\" once before, sitting inside आकाशः, the open sky. प्रकाशः (prakāśaḥ) is that very piece with pra-, \"forward\", in front of it — light as shining sent out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the sky and the light in it are built out of one word, parting only at the small piece each carries at the front. Ends in -अः."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Light, and the piece it shares with the sky."
            }
          ]
        },
